  "body": "https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/dom.html#palpable-content\r\n\r\n> This requirement is not a hard requirement, however, as there are many cases where an element can be empty legitimately, for example when it is used as a placeholder which will later be filled in by a script, or when the element is part of a template and would on most pages be filled in but on some pages is not relevant\\.\r\n> \r\n> Conformance checkers are encouraged to provide a mechanism for authors to find elements that fail to fulfill this requirement, as an authoring aid\\.\r\n\r\n\r\nThis is not entirely clear but most likely just human error; it looks as if _however_ is unneeded:\r\n\r\n This requirement is not a hard requirement, as there are many cases where an element can be empty legitimately, for example when it is used as a placeholder which will later be filled in by a script, or when the element is part of a template and would on most pages be filled in but on some pages is not relevant.\r\n\r\n_However_ , conformance checkers are encouraged to provide a mechanism for authors to find elements that fail to fulfill this requirement, as an authoring aid.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n",
